What is return ?
stops the execution of a function and returns a value.
function myFunction(name) {
  return "Hello " + name;
}
console.log(myFunction("dharshini")); // Hello dharshini

prompt()
built-in function used to display a dialog box that prompts the user for input. This dialog box includes a message, a text input field, and "OK" and "Cancel" buttons.
Syntax :
result = prompt(message, defaultValue);

